hadiths[47]{hadithnumber,text}:
"493","'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn Sa'id reported that his father said, \I waswith Salman when he visited a sick person in Kinda. When he went in"
"494","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \Affliction will continue to trouble the believers"
"495","A Bedouin came, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Has the fire of the Hell taken you? He said: What is the fire of the Hell? He said: It is a burning between the skin and the flesh. He said: No, he said: Have you been afflicted? He said: What is the affliction? He said: It is a stench that wafts in the head, breaks the bones, He said: No, he said: When he stood up, he said: Who would be pleased to look at a man from the people of the Fire, that is, let him look at it."
"496","Khalid bin al-Rabi, reported that when the illness of Huzayfah became serious his group and the Ansar heard of it. They visited him at night or in the (early) morning. Sayyidina Huzayfah asked, \What time is it?\"" They said"
"497","It is reported by Ayeshah that the Prophet said, \When a Believer falls ill"
"498","It is narrated by Ayeshah (ra) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said, \when a Muslim is afflicted by an anxiety"
"499","I was seriously ill at Makkah and the \nProphet visited me. I said to him \Messenger of Allah"
"500","It is narrated by Abdullah bin Amr that Prophet (ﷺ) said, \When a person falls ill then the reward of those deeds is also recorded for him which he used to perform when he was healthy."""
"501","Anas bin Maalik has reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) said, \When Allah involves a Muslim in bodily [pain then he is credited with a reward for those deeds which he was used to do when he was healthy as long as he is ill. Thus"
"502","Abu Hurayrah said that fever presented itself before the Holy Prophet (ﷺ). It said to him, ’’Send me to those people with whom you have a very deep connection. The Prophet (ﷺ) sent it to the Ansar. So, fever gripped them for six days and six nights. Their feverish condition became very serious and the Prophet visited them at their homes. Thy complained of fever and the Holy Prophet (ﷺ) went to each house and prayed for their health. When he was returning, one of their women followed behind him and said, \By Him who has sent you with the truth"
"503","Abu Hurayrah said that he did not like any illness more than fever because it went into each of his limbs. And, Allah grants each limb its share of reward."
"504","It is reported by Abu wail that someone said to Abu Nuhaylah (when he was ill), \Pray to Allah.\"" So"
"505","Ata bin Abu Rabah said that Ibn Abbas asked him if he would like him to show him a woman who would go to paradise. So, he said that he would certainly like (him to show him the woman). Ibn Abbas said to him. \This is a black woman who came to the Prophet and said to him"
"506","It is reported by Ibn Jurayj that Ata said to him, \I saw the woman"
"507","Abu Hurayrah reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying, \if a thorn pricks a Muslim in this world and he hopes for the reward against it then Allah forgives him his sins on the day of Resurrection\""."""
"508","It is narrated by Jabir that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say, \If a believing man or a believing woman or a Muslim man or Muslim woman falls ill then Allah"
"509","either\nyou will be killed and I will leave you to Allah or you will win and I\nwill be content. Beware of having your portion presented to you and then\nyou do not agree with it. Accept it, even though you dislike death.\""510"""
"510","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was ill, wearing a cloak. He placed his hand on him and found its heat above the cloak. Abu Sa'id said: ""How severe is your fever, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""We are like that; the trial is intensified for us and the reward is multiplied for us."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried?"" He said: ""The Prophets, then the righteous. One of them would be tried with poverty until he could find nothing but a cloak to wrap himself in and wear. And he would be tried with lice until they killed him. And one of them was more joyous at the trial than one of you is at ease."""
"511","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, who heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: ""I fell ill, so the Prophet ﷺ came to visit me, along with Abu Bakr, and they were both walking. They found me unconscious. The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution (wudu), then poured his ablution water over me, and I regained consciousness. There was the Prophet ﷺ, so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how should I deal with my wealth? How should I dispose of my wealth?' He did not answer me anything until the verse of inheritance was revealed."""
"512","Usama ibn Zayd reported that a child of one of the daughters of\nthe Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was very\nill. His mother sent word to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, to say that her child was dying. He told the messenger, \Go\nand tell her that to Allah belongs what He takes and what He gives. Everything\nis with Him until a stated term. She should be patient and leave him to\nAllah.\"" The messenger went back and told her. She sent to him again to\nplead with him to come. The Prophet"
"513","Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Abla said, \My wife was ill and I used to go to\nUmm ad-Darda'. She asked me"
"514","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, went to visit a bedouin when he was ill and said,\n\Do not worry. It is a purification if Allah so wills.\"" He said that the\nbedouin said"
"515","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, asked, \Which of you is fasting today?\"" Abu Bakr\nsaid"
"516","The Prophet entered upon Umm al-Sa'ib, and she was being treated with cupping. He said, ""What is wrong with you?"" She said, ""I have the fever, and Allah has humbled me."" The Prophet said, ""Leave it, do not treat it, for it removes the sins of the believer, just as the blacksmith removes rust from iron."""
"517","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \Allah says:'I asked you for food and you\ndid not feed Me. He (His slave) will say"
"518","Abu Sa'id reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \Visit the sick. Follow funeral processions. Remind yourselves\nof the Next World.\"""""
"519","to visit the sick, to attend funerals, and to say, 'may Allah\nhave mercy on you' when someone sneezes if he praises Allah Almighty.\""520"""
"520","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: ""Three men from Banu Sa'd narrated to me, each narrating from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Sa'd to visit him in Makkah. He (Sa'd) wept. He (the Prophet) said: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'I fear that I may die in the land from which I emigrated, just as Sa'd died.' He said: 'O Allah, heal Sa'd,' three times. He said: 'I have abundant wealth, and only my daughter inherits me. Shall I bequeath all my wealth?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then two-thirds?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then half?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Then one-third?' He said: 'One-third, and one-third is much. Indeed, your charity from your wealth is charity, and your spending on your family is charity, and what your wife eats from your food is charity for you. And that you leave your family well-off' — or he said: 'with a good livelihood — is better than leaving them begging people.' And he gestured with his hand."""
"521","Abu Qilaba reported from Abu'l-Ash'ath as-San'ani that Abu Asma'\nsaid, \Whoever visits his brother is in a tent of the Garden.\"" I (the transmitter)\nasked Abu Qilaba"
"522","Abu Bakr ibn Hazm and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir were some people\nfrom the mosque who visited 'Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Rafi' al-Ansari. They\nsaid, \Abu Hafs! Relate to us!\"" He said"
"523","'Ata' said, \Ibn 'Umar visited Ibn Safwan and the time came for\nthe prayer. So Ibn 'Umar prayed two rak'ats with them and then observed"
"524","Anas reported that a Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet, may\nAllah bless him and grant him peace. The boy became ill and the Prophet,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, went to visit him. He sat by his\nhead and said, \Become a Muslim.\"" The boy looked at his father who was\nalso sitting by his head. His father said to him"
"525","Isma'il b. Abi Waqqas narrated to us, Malik narrated to him, Hisham b. Urwa narrated to him from his father, from 'A'isha, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah came to Medina, Abu Bakr and Bilal were afflicted with a fever. I entered upon them and said: ""O Abu Bakr, how are you? O Bilal, how are you?"" Abu Bakr would say: ""Every man is in his best state in his home..."" And Bilal would say: ""Alas, if only my poetry were to be recited! I would not sleep a night... in a valley, with my water, my abundance, my abundance, and my water would return to its source... and I would be freed from my shame and my fatigue."" 'A'isha said: I came to the Messenger of Allah and informed him, and he said: ""O Allah, make Medina dear to us as Mecca is, or even more so. Purify it, and bless us in its good and its evil, and remove its fever, and make it like the Juhfah."""
"526","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, went to visit a bedouin who was ill. When the Prophet, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, visited someone who was ill, he would say,\n'There is no harm in it. It is a purification, Allah willing.\ That man\nthen said"
"527","Nafi' reported that when Ibn 'Umar visited someone who was ill,\nhe would ask him how he was. When he left him, he would say, \May Allah\nchoose what is best for you.\"" He did not say more than that."""
"528","'Amr ibn Sa'id said, \Al-Hajjaj visited Ibn 'Umar while I was with\nhim"
"529","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As said, \Do not visit wine-drinkers\nwhen they are ill.\"""""
"530","Al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari said, \I saw Umm ad-Darda' going to visit (a sick) Ansari man from the mosque and she was on her mount in an uncovered howdah.\"""""
"531","'Abdullah ibn Abi'l-Hudhayl said, \'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud went to\nvisit a sick person with some other people. There was a woman in the room\nand one of the men began to look at her"
"532","Zayd ibn Arqam said, \I had a pain in my eyes and the Prophet"
"533","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad reported that one of the Companions of Muhammad\nlost his eyesight and people visited him. He said, \I used to look at the\nProphet"
"534","Abdullah bin Salih and Ibn Yusuf narrated: Al-Layth narrated: Yazid bin al-Hadi narrated from Amr, the freed slave of al-Mutlib, from Anas, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""God, the Exalted, said: If I were to test him with his family, he would desire his family, then I would replace him with Paradise."""
"535","Abu Umama reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \Allah says"
"536","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would sit by his head when visiting the sick, then he would say seven times: ""I ask Allah, the Great, Lord of the Throne, to heal you. If there is a delay in your fate, may it be postponed from your destiny."""
"537","Ar-Rabi' ibn al-Hasan said, \I went with al-Hasan to visit Qatada.\nHe sat by his head and asked after him and made supplication for him. He\nsaid"
"538","He told us 'Abdullah bin Rajaa' and Hafs bin 'Umar, they said: He told us Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: I asked 'Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, ""What was the Prophet's behavior in his family?"" She said, ""He would be in the service of his family, and when prayer time came, he would go out."""
"539","Hisham ibn 'Urwa said that his father said, \I asked 'A'isha"
